---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Container from '../../components/Container.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Hack Make Do"
  description="This site sets no cookies and does not track you. This page explains what little data is involved when you visit or get in touch."
  currentPath="/privacy/"
>
  <PageHeader
    trail={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy' }]}
    title="Privacy"
    lead="This site sets no cookies and does not track you. This page explains what little data is involved when you visit or get in touch."
  />

  <section class="hmd-section hmd-section--flush-top" aria-label="Privacy notice">
    <Container variant="text">
      <Prose>
        <p><small>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11-19">19 November 2026</time></small></p>

        <h2 id="who">Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>
          Hack Make Do Limited, incorporated in England, company number 15432884, registered office Castle House,
          Castle Street, Guildford, GU1 3UW. Email <a href="mailto:warren@hackmakedo.com">warren@hackmakedo.com</a> 
          with any question about your data.
        </p>

        <h2 id="hosting">Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          This site is hosted on GitHub Pages and delivered through Cloudflare. Both handle your IP address to send
          you the pages and to protect the site from abuse.
        </p>

        <h2 id="analytics">Visitor statistics</h2>
        <p>Page views are counted with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which does not use cookies and does not identify you.</p>

        <h2 id="email">When you email me</h2>
        <p>I use your name, email address and message to reply and, if we work together, to run the project. I keep emails only as long as I need them for that, and to meet legal record-keeping duties.</p>

        <h2 id="video">Videos and code from YouTube, Vimeo, TED and GitHub</h2>
        <p>
          Videos on this site load nothing from YouTube, Vimeo or TED until you press play, and their preview images
          are served from this site. Once you press play, a YouTube video plays from youtube-nocookie.com, a Vimeo
          video plays from player.vimeo.com in its do-not-track mode, and a TED talk plays from embed.ted.com. That
          company may then store data on your device under its own privacy policy.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some posts show code kept on GitHub Gist. It loads from gist.github.com only when you press "Show code",
          and GitHub may then store data on your device under its own privacy policy.
        </p>

        <h2 id="settings">Remembering a setting</h2>
        <p>
          If you pause the scrolling banner on the home page, your browser remembers that in its own storage on your
          device, so the banner stays still next time. It holds only that setting, is never sent to me, and is removed
          when you press play again or clear this site's data.
        </p>

        <h2 id="fonts">Fonts and other files</h2>
        <p>Fonts and images are served from this site, so your browser does not contact a third party to show them.</p>

        <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under UK GDPR you can ask to see, correct or delete the personal data I hold about you. If you are
          unhappy with how I handle it, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office.
        </p>
      </Prose>
    </Container>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

